L50: 
L51: Parse command-line arguments into `Self`.
L52: 
L53: The primary one-stop-shop trait used to create an instance of a `clap` cite26†`Command` , conduct the parsing, and turn the resulting cite27†`ArgMatches` back into concrete instance of the user struct.
L54: This trait is primarily a convenience on top of cite17†`FromArgMatches` + cite18†`CommandFactory` which uses those two underlying traits to build the two fundamental functions `parse` which uses the `std::env::args_os` iterator, and `parse_from` which allows the consumer to supply the iterator (along with fallible options for each).
L55: 
L56: See also cite28†`Subcommand` and cite29†`Args` .
